sequenceDiagram
    participant Operator as Operator / SRE
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant ConfigMap as ConfigMap<br/>(llm-d-preflight-checks)
    participant Pod as vLLM Pod<br/>8000/TCP HTTP
    participant Preflight as preflight-checks.py
    participant VllmServe as vLLM serve

    rect rgb(230, 240, 255)
        Note over Operator, VllmServe: Flow 1: Preflight Check Injection
        Operator->>K8sAPI: kubectl apply ConfigMap<br/>HTTPS/443, TLS 1.2+, kubeconfig
        K8sAPI->>ConfigMap: Store preflight script
        Note over Pod: Container starts
        Pod->>Preflight: Execute preflight-checks.py
        Preflight->>Preflight: Collect GPU topology,<br/>NVLink, CPU, PCI, env vars
        alt LLMD_PREFLIGHT_CHECKS=pause
            Preflight->>Pod: Start HTTP server on 8000/TCP
            Note over Pod: Health probes satisfied<br/>GET /health → 200 OK
            Operator->>Pod: kubectl exec curl /exit<br/>HTTP/8000, No Auth
            Pod->>Preflight: Shutdown HTTP server
        end
        Preflight->>VllmServe: Chain to vLLM serve<br/>8000/TCP HTTP
    end

    participant ClientPod as Pod A<br/>(perftest server)
    participant TargetPod as Pod B<br/>(perftest client)

    rect rgb(255, 240, 230)
        Note over Operator, TargetPod: Flow 3: Network Performance Testing
        Operator->>K8sAPI: run-tests.py discovers pods<br/>HTTPS/443, kubeconfig
        K8sAPI-->>Operator: Pod list (label: llm-d.ai/model)
        Operator->>ClientPod: kubectl exec: start perftest server<br/>HTTPS/443
        Operator->>TargetPod: kubectl exec: run perftest client<br/>HTTPS/443
        TargetPod->>ClientPod: RDMA bandwidth test<br/>18515/TCP, ib_write_bw
        ClientPod-->>TargetPod: Bandwidth results
        Operator->>ClientPod: kubectl exec: start iperf3 server
        Operator->>TargetPod: kubectl exec: run iperf3 client
        TargetPod->>ClientPod: TCP/UDP throughput test<br/>5201/TCP
        ClientPod-->>TargetPod: Throughput results
        Note over Operator: Generate tabular + PNG reports
    end

    participant NIXLClient as nixl-client Pod<br/>GPU VRAM
    participant NIXLServerPod as nixl-server Pod<br/>5555/TCP ZMQ

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over NIXLClient, NIXLServerPod: Flow 2: NIXL Benchmark
        NIXLClient->>NIXLServerPod: ZMQ coordination<br/>5555/TCP, No Encryption
        NIXLClient->>NIXLServerPod: GPU VRAM-to-VRAM transfer<br/>UCX transport (RC/TCP), No Auth
        NIXLServerPod-->>NIXLClient: Transfer throughput results
    end
